@startuml codeemb-unixcoder
' UniXcoder: the paper's three prefix-selected modes (top, one of which the shipped
' path implicitly uses) versus what UniXcoderEmbedder actually feeds the graph
' (bottom). Muted = described by the paper but NOT emitted by libgrammstein.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/codeemb-unixcoder.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/code-embeddings/unixcoder.md.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #90A4AE
  FontColor #263238
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title UniXcoder — prefix-controlled modes (paper) vs. the shipped encoder-only path

package "Guo et al. 2022 — mode is selected by a prefix token" {
  rectangle "**⟨encoder-only⟩**\nbidirectional self-attention\n⇒ understanding: search, clone" as m1 #388E3C
  rectangle "**⟨decoder-only⟩**\ncausal self-attention\n⇒ generation: completion" as m2 #90A4AE
  rectangle "**⟨encoder-decoder⟩**\ncausal-prefix attention\n⇒ seq2seq: summarization" as m3 #90A4AE
  rectangle "**flattened AST + comments**\nlossless serialization used\nduring pre-training" as ast #90A4AE
}

package "libgrammstein — UniXcoderEmbedder::embed_code" {
  rectangle "**(code c, language ℓ)**\nℓ reaches only the cache key" as q #EF6C00
  rectangle "**Tokenizer**\nencode(c, true) — **raw code, no mode prefix**\ntruncate to max_length = 512" as tok #EF6C00
  rectangle "**ONNX RoBERTa encoder**\n125M params · 12 layers · d = 768" as enc #2E7D32
  rectangle "**CLS pooling**\nv = H₀ = data[..768]" as cls #2E7D32
  rectangle "**L2 normalize** → **v̂ ∈ ℝ⁷⁶⁸**" as out #455A64
}

m1 -[#90A4AE,dashed]-> enc : the mode the weights\nare used **as if** in
ast -[#90A4AE,dashed]-> tok : **not performed**\n(plain text in)

q --> tok
tok --> enc : (ids, mask)
enc --> cls
cls --> out

note bottom of tok #ECEFF1
  The shipped tokenizer call passes the code **verbatim**.
  It emits no ⟨encoder-only⟩ mode prefix, so the model is
  driven off-protocol relative to the paper. In practice the
  bidirectional export is already encoder-only, but a checkpoint
  that keys on the prefix will be under-conditioned.
end note

note right of cls #E8F5E9
  Contrastive pre-training (multi-modal
  contrastive learning + cross-modal
  generation) is what makes the CLS row
  a usable similarity vector.
end note

@enduml
